#define HELPCMD_STRING "Usage: ClaudeReader [options] [filename]\n\nClaudeReader - An e-comics reader (based on BDReader)\n\nGeneric options:\n   -h, --help\t\tShow help\n   -v, --version\tShow version information\n\nArguments:\n   filename\tComics file to open. Supported formats: PDF, EPUB, XPS, FB2, MOBI, CBR, CBZ, CBT, CB7, RAR, ZIP, TAR, 7Z and image folders.\n\nCommand line export:\n   -e, --export\t\tExport comics file as images\n\tUsage: ClaudeReader [-r] -e filename [export_folder] [format:.jpg/.png/.bmp] [panel: y/n] [page preview: y/n]\n\tExample: ClaudeReader -e Comics.pdf ./ExportedComics/ .jpg y n\n   -r, --rtl\t\tManga mode: read panels from right to left (put it before -e)\n\nStore:\n   --store list | <store> search \"query\" [page] | <store> chapters <manga id> | <store> pages <chapter id>\n   --store <store> download <manga id> <chapter id> [cbz|zip|pdf|images] [library folder]"
